{"id":"000VW2","title":"Mind the Edge ! #9","author":"Todd","solvedCount":5,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-05T15:34:04+00:00","posted":"Heute, 08:57 Uhr","rules":"Online play: https://sudokupad.app/1th1rr5bl1\n\nSudoku: Place digits 0–8 so that each digit appears exactly once in every row, column, and 3×3 box.\n\nEdge mines: On an ordinary cell, the digit equals the total number of mines on its four edges (top, bottom, left, right). Each edge holds 0, 1, or 2 mines.\n\nSpecial cells: There are exactly 9 special cells, one in each row, each column, and each 3×3 box. The digits in the special cells are 0–8, each once. A special digit differs from its four-edge mine sum by exactly 1: it may be one higher or one lower.\n\nGiven edges: The four edges of each given digit are marked.\n\n• blue = 0 mines\n\n• red = 1 mine\n\n• red with a red × = 2 mines\n\nAll other edges are unmarked and must be deduced. Mark remaining edges yourself (Pen tool under Settings ⚙).\n\nTIPS: This is a hybrid of Sudoku and Minesweeper. You need both Sudoku rules and the fact that adjacent digits share the mine count on their common edge. On an ordinary cell, an 8 forces 2 mines on each of its four edges, so none of its four neighbors can be 0 or 1. Likewise, none of the four neighbors of an ordinary 0 can be 7 or 8. A special digit is one higher or one lower than its four-edge mine sum, so those two examples apply only to ordinary cells. The figure below shows one possible arrangement of ordinary digits in a box, together with mines on edges:\n\nMind the Edge ! #0: 000VE7.\n\nMind the Edge ! #2: 000UZC.\n\nMind the Edge ! #3: 000V0U.\n\nMind the Edge ! #5: 000VES.\n\nMind the Edge ! #6: 000VF7.\n\nMind the Edge ! #7: 000VLQ.\n\nMind the Edge ! #8: 000VR5.\n\nMore of my games: hitodd.com.","solutionCode":"Enter the digits in the special cells from box 1 to box 9.","tags":["Sudoku","Minesweeper"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/1th1rr5bl1","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":""